---
description: Rules for test and fixture files
globs: ["**/test/**", "**/src/test/**", "conformance/**", "**/*.test.ts"]
alwaysApply: false
---
- Each `Done when` line in the spec becomes at least one test. Each `Refuses` line becomes a negative test.
- No `Date.now()`, argument-less `new Date()`, `Math.random()`, `System.currentTimeMillis()`, or unseeded `Random`.
- No `.only`, `.skip`, `it.todo`, `xit`, `xdescribe`. `@Disabled` needs a reason comment on the line above.
- Never remove or change an existing line. Never delete or rename a test or fixture file.
- Fake secrets are built by string concatenation.
- A new test must fail on an assertion before the code exists, not on an import error.
